1
00:00:02,503 --> 00:00:05,797
<i>Your first chakra
is the Root Chakra,</i>

2
00:00:05,923 --> 00:00:09,343
<i>which deals with fear
and survival.</i>

3
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:10,594
<i>What scares you?</i>

4
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:15,933
I'm afraid of being seen
as the Avatar.

5
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:18,769
<i>The Dome's kinda like
the granddaddy</i>

6
00:00:18,894 --> 00:00:20,437
<i>of the Anomalies, right?</i>

7
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:22,021
<i>If we connect with it,</i>

8
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:24,107
<i>we'll be sucked back
into that memory.</i>

9
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:26,984
<i>What did you see?
Just tell me!</i>

10
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:29,404
<i>Please, I need you to trust me.</i>

11
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:31,907
<i>I'm doing this
for the both of us.</i>

12
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:34,743
Nisha!

13
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:48,256
Mom?

14
00:00:48,257 --> 00:00:49,882
Come along, silly furball.

15
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:54,096
You're lucky we didn't leave
without you.

16
00:00:54,221 --> 00:00:55,596
This is the past.

17
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:58,308
That dome brought us
into the Memory Void!

18
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:00,561
Pavi, we shouldn't be here.

19
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:02,271
Karthik and Jae need us!

20
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:04,147
We don't have time for this!

21
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:05,857
We couldn't leave without Geet.

22
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:07,858
It's Dad!

23
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:10,069
You said you're done
chasing ghosts!

24
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:12,572
But the answers are right here!

25
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:15,200
We can finally find out
where Mom and Dad are!

26
00:01:15,701 --> 00:01:16,618
But--

27
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,209
<i>Fire.</i>

28
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:25,586
<i>Air.</i>

29
00:01:25,961 --> 00:01:27,004
<i>Water.</i>

30
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:28,755
<i>Earth.</i>

31
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:32,174
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,</i>

32
00:01:32,175 --> 00:01:34,303
<i>master of all four elements,</i>

33
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:36,597
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

34
00:01:36,722 --> 00:01:39,515
<i>Out of the devastation,
the world built</i>

35
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:41,309
<i>the Seven Havens.</i>

36
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:43,269
<i>Now the Avatar has returned,</i>

37
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:46,231
<i>but for the first time,
there are two.</i>

38
00:01:46,732 --> 00:01:49,317
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again...</i>

39
00:01:49,318 --> 00:01:52,321
<i>but I believe
they will save it.</i>

40
00:02:00,287 --> 00:02:01,579
Stay calm, people!

41
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:03,915
We're evacuating
as fast as we can!

42
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:07,210
Move it!
Don't you dolts wanna live?!

43
00:02:07,336 --> 00:02:08,419
Over here!

44
00:02:08,544 --> 00:02:09,837
Keep moving!

45
00:02:19,306 --> 00:02:21,390
Commander! We should retreat!

46
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:22,934
I need to get the girls!

47
00:02:30,025 --> 00:02:30,817
Commander!

48
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:39,742
We--

49
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:42,078
Kayoko-- The Avatar--

50
00:02:42,079 --> 00:02:43,788
I-I don't--

51
00:02:43,789 --> 00:02:46,540
It's okay, Jae,
your personal hero is losing it.

52
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:49,460
Don't panic.

53
00:02:49,461 --> 00:02:52,964
Listen up! If anyone
can handle this energy,

54
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:54,590
it's the Avatar.

55
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:57,803
We need to focus on getting
folks out of the haven.

56
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,472
You're right.

57
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:02,391
Thank you, Jae.

58
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:04,309
I lost sight of my purpose.

59
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,811
Where do we stand? Report!

60
00:03:06,812 --> 00:03:08,146
The Brigade is scattered.

61
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:09,981
There are thousands
who need to get out.

62
00:03:10,107 --> 00:03:11,900
It's... not looking great.

63
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,317
Come on, Lan!

64
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:14,652
Uki didn't reunite with us

65
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:16,321
just to see the haven fail!

66
00:03:17,823 --> 00:03:18,907
You didn't, right?

67
00:03:19,366 --> 00:03:20,951
That would be a weird choice.

68
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:23,495
Will you help us, Agam?

69
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,288
I know Ellora
isn't your favorite place.

70
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:29,000
Oh, I'd hate to lose
my father's bakery.

71
00:03:29,418 --> 00:03:33,839
And it might be inconvenient
if you all perish.

72
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:35,715
We can do this.

73
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:36,883
Spread through the district,

74
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:39,427
let other benders know
of the evacuation.

75
00:03:39,428 --> 00:03:42,722
Like a mighty wind racing
through the canyons.

76
00:03:42,723 --> 00:03:44,266
For the survival of Ellora!

77
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:46,600
For the survival of Ellora!

78
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:48,770
Yeah, I'm not saying that.

79
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:52,149
Come on, Zi!
The Republic Forest awaits!

80
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:55,444
I'm going back.

81
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:57,653
For that waterbender guy?

82
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:59,239
Someone's got a crush.

83
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:01,741
Well, if you're planning
on doing something stupid,

84
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:03,034
you gotta take us.

85
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:17,841
I'm sorry, Nisha.

86
00:04:18,841 --> 00:04:20,802
This is for the best.

87
00:04:26,475 --> 00:04:29,728
Is it breakfast already, Mama?

88
00:04:32,731 --> 00:04:34,733
Shh, my tiny gem.

89
00:04:35,192 --> 00:04:36,568
We're going on a trip.

90
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:38,904
Let your sister rest.

91
00:04:41,031 --> 00:04:42,741
Why isn't Nisha coming?

92
00:04:43,325 --> 00:04:46,076
Someone's on their way
to get Nisha some help.

93
00:04:46,077 --> 00:04:47,579
Why?

94
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:49,371
What's wrong with her?

95
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:50,624
No more questions, Pavi.

96
00:04:50,749 --> 00:04:51,750
Come along.

97
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:14,355
We just... left you?

98
00:05:17,609 --> 00:05:19,236
Pavi?

99
00:05:19,361 --> 00:05:21,780
You getting a kachori?

100
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:29,788
Pavi...?

101
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:35,794
Mom!

102
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:44,803
I don't understand...

103
00:05:45,387 --> 00:05:47,721
why would our parents do this?

104
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:49,181
I-It doesn't matter.

105
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:51,810
Let's just go back home! Please!

106
00:05:52,936 --> 00:05:54,061
No.

107
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:55,313
Something's wrong.

108
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:20,630
You need to leave this area
as soon as possible.

109
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:22,673
Where's Uki?

110
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:24,967
- Did we lose her already?
- Sorry,

111
00:06:24,968 --> 00:06:27,387
Ma needed to bring
all her cast iron pans.

112
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:29,764
The seasoning on this pan
is priceless!

113
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:32,893
Jae! I packed you fritters!

114
00:06:33,018 --> 00:06:35,561
Uh... t-thanks, Ahnah!

115
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:37,147
This way! Come on!

116
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,358
Hey!

117
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:43,694
It's the Brigade kid
I almost clobbered!

118
00:06:43,695 --> 00:06:45,863
Where are those twins?

119
00:06:45,864 --> 00:06:47,866
Hopefully, saving us all.

120
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:55,874
Look! There's Mom and Dad!

121
00:06:57,959 --> 00:06:59,543
The storm is blinding!

122
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:00,794
We should go back!

123
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:03,088
We have to wait for Nisha!

124
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:04,299
No! We keep going!

125
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:05,884
We can't--

126
00:07:12,057 --> 00:07:14,058
Why would you leave me?!

127
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:19,939
Go back to the house, Nisha!

128
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,982
Your power is too dangerous!

129
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,442
No!

130
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:31,409
Pavi!

131
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,293
- Ahh!
- Pavi!

132
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:42,003
Don't let go!

133
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:44,005
I won't!

134
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:45,923
Pramodh, we need to stop!

135
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:48,509
I won't let her destroy
our family!

136
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:50,052
Please wait!

137
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:52,514
Don't leave me!

138
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:55,140
Nisha! Nisha, no!

139
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:56,517
We have to go back!

140
00:07:56,518 --> 00:07:58,686
No, no, no! Please!

141
00:07:58,687 --> 00:08:00,854
Please!

142
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:13,743
Nisha, stop this right now!

143
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:22,544
- Nisha!
- Run! Don't look back!

144
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:25,046
No! Pavi!

145
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:13,553
Pavi...

146
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:15,221
All this time,

147
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:18,933
I've tried to learn
what happened to our parents.

148
00:09:19,059 --> 00:09:21,227
Pavi, I-I didn't mean to--

149
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:23,063
You kept this from me.

150
00:09:23,605 --> 00:09:26,149
You didn't want me to find out.

151
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:29,360
<i>You</i> are what happened to them.

152
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:38,243
Everyone, keep calm!

153
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:40,789
The Energy Dome responds
to your fear!

154
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:52,091
Okay, maybe I don't care
if you all perish!

155
00:10:02,268 --> 00:10:05,188
I rounded up your silly benders
for you.

156
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:06,355
You're welcome.

157
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:07,981
Whoa, Zi!

158
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,274
It's me, Daemin!

159
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:10,902
Remember? From jail?

160
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:13,613
Ha! Ya know, she asked me
on a date.

161
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:18,117
You didn't leave me to die?

162
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:21,203
What sort of worthless bandit
are you?

163
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:33,591
The Faceless are ready,
Commander.

164
00:10:36,344 --> 00:10:38,554
I know we've fought
on opposite sides,

165
00:10:38,555 --> 00:10:40,140
believe different ideals,

166
00:10:40,265 --> 00:10:42,559
but let's stand united now

167
00:10:42,684 --> 00:10:44,227
to protect one another.

168
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:46,271
- For the survival of--
- Ugh!

169
00:10:46,396 --> 00:10:48,523
Enough, Brigade Boy!

170
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:49,606
...Ellora.

171
00:10:53,611 --> 00:10:57,740
Pavi, please,
just let me explain.

172
00:10:58,158 --> 00:10:59,616
I just couldn't let that--

173
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:03,163
I thought Mom and Dad left me
because I was the Avatar.

174
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:04,873
A monster.

175
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:06,875
But they weren't scared of me.

176
00:11:07,876 --> 00:11:10,962
They were scared of you!

177
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:36,279
Ruhi! Good girl.

178
00:11:56,299 --> 00:11:59,051
Leave her alone!

179
00:12:11,648 --> 00:12:15,400
My whole life
I've lived in fear!

180
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:17,320
Scared of what I really am!

181
00:12:18,071 --> 00:12:20,990
But I'm sick of being afraid!

182
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:24,243
I know I can survive!

183
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:38,091
I am the Avatar!

184
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:58,443
There's a second Avatar?!

185
00:12:58,444 --> 00:12:59,862
- She's fighting back!
- She's on our side!

186
00:12:59,988 --> 00:13:01,697
Are the girls all right?

187
00:13:01,698 --> 00:13:03,824
Wait, is that Pavi?!

188
00:13:03,825 --> 00:13:07,203
Not just a trash gremlin
after all.

189
00:13:08,079 --> 00:13:10,915
Go! I can handle this!

190
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:14,209
You heard her!
Everybody, go! Go!

191
00:13:24,846 --> 00:13:27,473
Pavi... how are you doing this?

192
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:59,297
Winds guide me.

193
00:14:57,063 --> 00:14:58,563
I remember this.

194
00:14:59,649 --> 00:15:01,442
Ahh!

195
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:20,795
Avatar Korra?

196
00:15:22,255 --> 00:15:23,005
Huh.

197
00:15:23,131 --> 00:15:25,133
You don't look scary up close.

198
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:41,816
My Root Chakra has unblocked?

199
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,234
Why?

200
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:45,570
Oh.

201
00:15:45,695 --> 00:15:48,071
Because I let go of my fear

202
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:50,491
and accepted being the Avatar.

203
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:55,413
My second chakra...?

204
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:05,923
Is that... the Floating Isles?

205
00:16:07,425 --> 00:16:08,801
Are they in trouble?

206
00:16:11,888 --> 00:16:13,598
Guess I'm doing this alone.

207
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:34,243
Pavi saved them all...

208
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:36,871
without me.

209
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:48,841
Pavi! You-you did it!

210
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:53,553
And... a-and I'm so, so sorry
I didn't tell you!

211
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:55,723
I-I was terrified you'd...

212
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,642
you'd...

213
00:16:57,767 --> 00:17:00,186
you'd... leave me.

214
00:17:03,356 --> 00:17:06,316
What happened
to "Twin Promise," Nisha?!

215
00:17:06,317 --> 00:17:09,153
How could you do that
to your family?

216
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:11,030
To me?

217
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:13,699
I-I...

218
00:17:15,201 --> 00:17:16,327
I don't know.

219
00:17:19,329 --> 00:17:21,248
Pavi, Nisha!

220
00:17:21,249 --> 00:17:22,415
Finally!

221
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:27,171
I won't be a destroyer like you.

222
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,799
I'll be a better Avatar.

223
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:32,008
Geet, scramble!

224
00:17:33,261 --> 00:17:34,386
I'll go after her.

225
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:35,720
Bring her back.

226
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:36,888
We need to understand

227
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:39,100
how she expelled
the spirit energy.

228
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:47,107
Oh, I'm so relieved you're okay.

229
00:17:47,108 --> 00:17:49,735
You're not mad at me?

230
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,736
Nisha, I'm proud of you.

231
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:54,197
You held back the Dome
and gave us a chance

232
00:17:54,198 --> 00:17:55,824
to get people out of the haven.

233
00:17:55,825 --> 00:17:59,370
Because of you and Pavi,
Ellora is safe.

234
00:18:02,123 --> 00:18:03,791
Pavi!

235
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,293
Where are you?

236
00:18:05,835 --> 00:18:08,670
I just wanna understand
what happened!

237
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:17,888
I was just saving a bug, Jae.

238
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:19,472
What?

239
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:20,682
The day we met.

240
00:18:20,683 --> 00:18:23,728
For years, I kept my head down,

241
00:18:23,853 --> 00:18:25,313
staying invisible.

242
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:29,274
But then you found me.

243
00:18:29,275 --> 00:18:31,026
I met my secret twin,

244
00:18:31,027 --> 00:18:32,986
got pulled into the White Lotus,

245
00:18:32,987 --> 00:18:36,073
and... now everyone knows
I'm an Avatar.

246
00:18:38,868 --> 00:18:40,328
Yeah,

247
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:42,121
that sounds like a lot.

248
00:18:44,915 --> 00:18:48,628
I don't know what happened
when I took in that energy,

249
00:18:48,753 --> 00:18:50,421
but I'm not meant to stay here.

250
00:18:51,005 --> 00:18:52,590
What are you talking about?

251
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:56,969
I saw the past Avatars, sort of.

252
00:18:57,428 --> 00:19:00,723
And I opened one of my chakras,

253
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:03,184
but I think the rest
are still blocked?

254
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:05,393
I don't know,
it's Avatar journey stuff.

255
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:07,188
There were a lot of shiny stars!

256
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:11,692
I think I'm needed
in another haven.

257
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:14,320
Okay.

258
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:16,029
Wow.

259
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:17,865
A cosmic mission.

260
00:19:18,449 --> 00:19:20,325
Let's report to Karthik and--

261
00:19:20,326 --> 00:19:22,036
I'm not going back, Jae.

262
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:26,457
Are things all right with Nisha?

263
00:19:27,083 --> 00:19:30,670
No. I don't know
if they ever will be again.

264
00:19:32,755 --> 00:19:34,298
My mission starts now.

265
00:19:34,799 --> 00:19:37,885
Just give me a head start
before you tell Karthik,

266
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:39,470
okay?

267
00:19:44,058 --> 00:19:45,393
You want some company?

268
00:19:46,686 --> 00:19:48,187
Pretty lonely out there.

269
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:51,064
Last time I checked,

270
00:19:51,065 --> 00:19:53,316
Brigade Boys don't go
on dangerous adventures

271
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:55,152
into the Harshlands.

272
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:58,364
I don't think
I'm that Jae anymore.

273
00:20:00,658 --> 00:20:03,368
<i>Before I met you,
all I wanted out of life</i>

274
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:05,996
<i>was to be the best
Brigade bender I could be,</i>

275
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,666
<i>to do my duty to Ellora.</i>

276
00:20:09,709 --> 00:20:12,378
<i>I just wanted to keep
my home strong.</i>

277
00:20:12,503 --> 00:20:13,838
<i>Keep it surviving.</i>

278
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:18,134
<i>My whole life I was taught
to hate the Avatar.</i>

279
00:20:18,801 --> 00:20:22,096
<i>Then, everything got turned
upside down.</i>

280
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:27,810
<i>Now, an Avatar
is one of my favorite people.</i>

281
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:31,980
<i>I know the future looks
pretty bleak right now,</i>

282
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:36,109
<i>but I for one am glad
you're not invisible anymore.</i>

283
00:20:36,110 --> 00:20:39,280
<i>If there is a light
at the end of this tunnel,</i>

284
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:41,323
<i>it's you, Pavi.</i>

285
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:45,243
<i>Is it scary that I'm not
on the path I started?</i>

286
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,202
<i>Heck yeah!</i>

287
00:20:46,203 --> 00:20:47,787
<i>But that's okay.</i>

288
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:50,958
<i>This</i> is <i>the path
I'm meant to be on.</i>

289
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:55,629
<i>I'm not sure about much
right now,</i>

290
00:20:55,755 --> 00:20:56,964
<i>except for one thing:</i>

291
00:20:58,090 --> 00:21:00,843
<i>you're the key to fixing
this world.</i>

292
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:04,054
<i>And I'll be by your side</i>

293
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:05,431
<i>the whole way.</i>

294
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:07,391
That is...

295
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:08,809
if you'll let me.

296
00:21:10,436 --> 00:21:13,396
Ugh, fine, you can come!

297
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:15,064
But I'm in charge!

298
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:17,026
Then Geet. Then you.

299
00:21:18,611 --> 00:21:19,487
Fair enough.

300
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:21,197
Lead the way.

301
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:37,338
Pavi...

302
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:45,054
Hurry up, Jae!

303
00:21:45,179 --> 00:21:48,348
It's a long walk and I have half
as many feet as you!

304
00:21:48,349 --> 00:21:49,600
Coming!

